        <p>gitZP,Dbod •erey, Y wonders how the Pearson Potter' Company Iki sell 100 nieces of crockery for one guinea 4,,:licerx6t a post card at once, and send for list. A beauti- itta:., Ite• ilierviee. a China tea service, jugs, basins, dishes 1)(-)Zeit, T.Verybody pleasurably surprised, All for one %.,. You wish to save money, write to the PEARSON 1,, Ibe h ,".. nanley, for particulars.—Advt, •, ,I 8...4-, UV. -1. . . ma t. ut Edinburgh, when a midshipman, used, it , a.pd , 0 Put it nut the Queen's signature out of his letters uP try auction. ...—Mrs. Winslow's Soothing Syrup has bee Years by millions of mothers for their children with perfect success. It will relieve the poor ilately. It is pleasant to taste ; it produces " 'leeP, by relieving the child from pain. and the cubis, awakes "as brights as albutton." Of all V+. per bottle.—Ada.</p>
