        <p>nection with this question. That the recent horrors to which the-defencel Armenians have been subjected were-not Ør ess the result of a casual outbreak of gallon:one- dan fanaticism has now been thorouglil37' proved. Ontrages of a similar character hasl• marked the whole period of Turkish rule.la 11 a E s uropean observer in the province, Of Ve ,„is• prepared a list of enormities which brings fact out with painful clearness. Ho; tells us/ '7l' " instance, that the Pasha who has been,entroBt with the government of Van is responsibli3v directly or indirectly, for the death of no feW4. r - than one thousand Christians and for the ePstris ozon of five thousand more. This precious reFfeci sentative of Turkish " law and order" is hand ta glove with the thievish and murderous Fairds these latter gentry consequently know they will escape punishment no. mat crime they may be guilty of. The firsb conireli c's sioner of the police in this same, provln°, ;:'S worthy colleague of his nominal chief,. " said that if" the history of the life of this during the last three years could be written would horrify the Christian world, beyond Melly sure." The so-called courts of justice are res 0.. instruments by means of which the most shsratte less and heartless injnstice is inflicted upen communities of Armenian Christians. nr 'e or ample, in the summer of 193, four men and girls were collecting herbs on the hillside near at, party Armenian village, when they were set of armed Kurds. The mon were' slain and mutilated and the girls were treated the most outrageous fashion. Bare, it Inigths have been thought, was a case in which ,hs. Turkish authorities would step in to protect_liat. people whom they are supposed to govern. what was the sequel? There could be no dein; of the fact that murders had been committed, his Excellency the Governor allowed hirnseltY; be persuaded that the whole affair was a plot:be the part of the Aemenians themselves, antlosa result was not only that no Kurds were pul'i .00 but that even up to the present time there ale; of Armenians in the local prison on the °largos, being concerned in the murder. There sea co indeed, to. be no end to the cruel and uniFist :ish which can be laid to the charge of the Turtaio ,2ulers of Armenia, and it will be a serious sore upon the honour of Christian countries, of 13ur they allow this state of things to continue. merciless. 0</p>
