        <p>BOWLING. AsSOCir LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE COUNT+. • TION. reetiag CHAMPIONSHIP Arm ASSOCIATION TIES.-"'no 14,A at ..,r116,1 of the council of the County Associstion, Spread Eagle Hotel, Manchester, on Tuesday n'' J. J. Meakin, president, in the chair, the secret J.Singleton, reported that of the 16 ties in the ary round for the club championship, 11 played off over neutral greens, and that Didsburv, Hindsford, Sefton Park, Le' and ton received a walk over. The other successin, titors were :—Douglas, Withington, Cheetharn perley, Broughton (Cobden), Wigan, IlarPur two Warrington and the two Pendleton. In response to allommunication from Yorksbn the inter-county match at Mirfield• solved that the names of playerS and 1 Higher the Lancashire team must be sent in to tary prior to the evening of the Mt Jann't the. match commence at noon on the 29th of Prior to the draw for the next series of ries' dent impressed on the representatives importance of getting them trundled off as sible, as playing on the last day allowed frequently occasisned much inconvenience. resulted as follows :—Championship : Warril4 v. Warrington South, at Newton.le-VVillows ; V. Wigan, at Urmston Victoria; Douglas V. (Cobden), at Didsbury ; Pendleton (Woolpanci ham Hill, at Broughton • Timperley % Northenden ; Pendleton (Horseshoe) Urmston ; Hindsford v. Higher Broughton• ham; Sefton Park v. Levenshulme, at Wigan* Lion ties :—Stretford v. Chorlten-curn-Elard, verley ; Cheetham V. Leigh, at Pendleton _ Urmston (Victoria) v. Newton, at Warrington, Walton v. Brooklands, at Warrington South , (Nelson) v. Northenden, at Levenshulme ; Cr" v. Broughton, at Chorlton Green; Choritorler Whalley Range, at Broughton (Cobden). r of thanks to the Chairman, proposed by gr. Coombs, the meeting adjourned to the 26th Jae</p>
