        <p>WEEKLY CHAT.—Subject : Second-hand Furniture.— The opening of Spring is the time for the busy house- wife to put her house in ora er, therefore the matter of furni- shing must be well discussed. We cannot, therefore, do better than advise a visit to Worsley's before definitely de- ciding where and what to purchase. This visit cannot pos- sibly but prove remunerative, if only in experience. " The Pantheon ' being a hive of Industry, it is a palatial pile of buildings close to the Central Station. having a frontage ot nearly 150 feet. This immense building is filled horn floor to ceiling (six storeys) 'with the grandest collection of High- class Second-hand Furniture In the World Thiq ir= no', an exaggeration, but can be verified by ocular el emonbtr,tt mu if you pay a visit to Manchester. Suites of Bedroom Furni- ture, for instance, by such makers as Goodall, Lamb, Ogden, dtc., original cost horn £2OO to £3OO, for from £5O to £7O ; suites, original cost £5O to £7O, for £lO to £2O. Pay a visit and see for yourself ; you can surely use your common sense, and see if Worsley's is the place as described.</p>
        <p>TO COUNTRY BUYERS—The enormoits patronage en- 1. by Worsley's from customers all over Lancashire, Yorkshire, Cheshire, The Potteries, all over the North, The Midlaads, and Wales, will prove how much is the saving effected by purchasing at Worsley's. In future carriage will be paid on all orders over £2O to any part of England and Wales. It is only fair to say that better value could not be obtained than Worsley's New Goods and the Second-band Furniture simply bewilders and demoralises competition. Never mind what distance 3ou live from Manchester, it will pay you to visit Worsley's ; you will save quite 50 per cent.</p>
        <p>(IAUTION.—Beware of buying new London jerrybuilt fur- ) niture, no matter how low the price is— it is dear at any price. Worsley's have second-hand reliable furniture by good makers, which will last for ages. There is no disputing the fact that high-claris second-hand furniture is better than new. The only fault is that sometimes the article is old- fashioned. This is easily remedied at Worsley's, they having over 50 cabinet makers at work modernising second-hand fur- niture when necessary. For instance, second-hand, side- boards are easily modernised by having the hacks raised, the plates bevellea. and the panels carved. You never need fear cracking, blistering, grub eaten, or moth eaten furniture at Worsley's. Second-hand furniture is not troubled with these complaints. They give a written warranty for 10 years with all furnishhing orders.</p>
        <p>f\YEW FURNITURE.—AII Worsley's new furniture is their 4.1 own make. Of course it is obviously impossible to sup- ply every requirement second-hand, Worsley's have, there- fore, erected a Cabinet Works in City-road, with an Immense stock of seasoned timber for the production of reliable furni- ture. Every item in the Bedding Department is new, guiran- teed pure, under minute inspection.</p>
